Finding: {"title":"generate-stage does not validate stageIdx lower bound — negative index causes undefined stage crash","severity":"LOW","area":"Input validation","files":["src/server/routes/routes-ai-curriculum-incremental.ts"],"detail":"Line 595-598: `const stageIdx = body.stageIdx ?? build.currentStageIdx; if (stageIdx >= outline.stages.length) return 400;` — only the upper bound is checked. A caller passing `stageIdx: -1` (or any negative integer) passes this guard, then `outline.stages[stageIdx]` at line 600 evaluates to `undefined`, and `targetStage.name` on line 611 (via buildStagePrompt call) throws a TypeError, producing an unhandled 500 instead of a clean 400.","impact":"Low-severity crash/500 on malformed input rather than a clean validation error; not exploitable beyond a minor DoS-by-error-spam or confusing error message, since requireAuth() already gates the endpoint.","recommendation":"Change the guard to `if (stageIdx < 0 || stageIdx >= outline.stages.length) return c.json({ error: 'Stage index out of range' }, 400);`","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

